# Root-level ignores. jarvis-app/ has its own; this covers the repo root,
# where an npm run from the wrong directory used to leave stray files that
# got committed by accident (a vitest cache landed in git this way).
# The trailing slash matters and was missing the case that bit: "node_modules/"
# matches a DIRECTORY only, so a node_modules SYMLINK (which is what a git
# worktree gets, pointed at the real install so every worktree shares one copy)
# is not ignored, and a `git add -A` in that worktree commits three symlinks.
# Checking that commit out into the real repo then replaces the real
# node_modules with a link to itself and takes the toolchain down with it.
# Both forms, so neither shape can be added again.
node_modules/
node_modules
dist/
*.log

# Sandbox scratch: staging tarballs and bundles are transport, never source.
*.tar.gz
*.bundle
